readme_title = md`# SoundScript

This module connects SoundScript to the notebook: the cell language registered with the editor, the listings and the inspector. The checker and compiler are in \`@tomlarkworthy/soundscript-checker\` and the library that compiled cells call is in \`@tomlarkworthy/soundscript-runtime\`. It does not need the tutorial module; a notebook can keep this one and drop the other.

Four SoundScript cells and a view that uses them:`
// %%
readme_listing = cellListing(ss_module, invalidation, { from: "tally", to: "doubled" })
// %%
//ss: ./core-example.ts
// %%
example_view = htl.html`<div class="ss-example"><button onclick=${() => bump()}>bump</button> <button onclick=${() => reset()}>reset</button> <code>tally = ${tally}</code>, <code>doubled = ${doubled}</code></div>`
// %%
readme_example = md`\`tally\` is state. \`bump\` and \`reset\` are actions, the only places it is written. \`doubled\` reads it. Open any of them with its **edit** bar. An edit is always stored; a cell that does not check does not run.`
// %%
readme_use = ss_highlightCode(md`## Using it in a module

To write SoundScript cells in another module of this notebook, import each capability your cells name:

\`\`\`
import { ss_now, ss_random, ss_log, ss_fetch, ss_source } from "@tomlarkworthy/soundscript"
import { ss_pool } from "@tomlarkworthy/soundscript-workers"   // only in a module with a cell that takes pool
\`\`\`

A compiled cell takes each cell of \`@tomlarkworthy/soundscript-runtime\` that it uses as an input of its own, named \`ss_<name>\`: \`ss_action\` for a cell that calls \`action\`, \`ss_ref\` for a state cell. The build and the editor add \`import {action as ss_action} from "@tomlarkworthy/soundscript-runtime"\` when a cell first needs it, and leave it when no cell does any more. A plain cell takes none. The checker and compiler are \`soundscript\` of \`@tomlarkworthy/soundscript-checker\`, which the tooling cells of this module use. Add a cell after a SoundScript cell and type a source such as \`const total = (a: number, b: number) => a + b;\`. The editor's header shows the language the cell is stored in. Picking another language there changes the view, not the cell: a SoundScript cell viewed as Observable JavaScript shows its compiled cell text, which cannot be saved from that view, and an Observable JavaScript cell viewed as SoundScript shows \`const <name> = (<inputs>) => <body>;\`, which Shift-Enter stores as SoundScript if it checks. A view that cannot be made (text that does not parse, a \`viewof\` or \`mutable\` cell, a cell with no name, an import, a cell that uses \`this\`) leaves the text as it was and shows the reason beside the picker. A SoundScript cell is checked against the module's other SoundScript cells and, if it is \`ok\`, compiled and defined. A module whose cells call \`compile\` also defines \`ss_compile\`:

\`\`\`
ss_compile = soundscript.compiler(() => ss_source(my_module))
viewof my_module = thisModule()   // from @tomlarkworthy/runtime-sdk
\`\`\``)
// %%
readme_capabilities = md`## Capabilities

A capability parameter becomes an input on one of this module's variables:

| parameter | variable |
|---|---|
| \`now\` | \`ss_now\` |
| \`random\` | \`ss_random\` |
| \`fetch\` | \`ss_fetch\` |
| \`log\` | \`ss_log\` |
| \`pool\` | \`ss_pool\` of the add-on \`@tomlarkworthy/soundscript-workers\`, not of this module (workers start when a cell that takes \`pool\` first runs) |
| \`compile\` | \`ss_compile\`, defined by the module that uses it |
| \`invalidation\` | the runtime's own \`invalidation\` |`
// %%
readme_storage = md`## How a cell is recognised and stored

A cell compiles to ordinary JavaScript: one runtime variable, or two for a state cell. In a state cell, \`viewof tally\` holds the handle and \`tally\` holds the value. A parameter \`tally: State<number>\` is an input on \`viewof tally\`. The \`viewof\` name makes the notebook's tools group the pair as one cell.

A variable is SoundScript when the first comment in its definition is the marker \`/*{lang:"ss"}*/\`. The definition keeps the types as \`/*ss:…*/\` comments. It keeps JSX as \`/*ss<…*/\` comments beside the lowered \`h(...)\` calls. The typed source is therefore recovered from the definition text alone, and it survives a save (\`test_ss_roundtrip\`).`
// %%
readme_memo = md`## When a cell runs

A plain cell compiles to its function applied to its inputs, an ordinary Observable cell, and the Observable runtime decides when it runs: when it is first read, and again whenever one of its inputs was computed again. The runtime does not compare values, so a cell whose input was recomputed to the same value still runs. A cell that calls a built-in or reads a cell of another language has the same shape and also takes the runtime cells it uses (\`ss_action\`, \`ss_cross\`). A state cell is \`ss_ref(this, name, inputs, fn)\`, an events cell \`ss_events(this, name, inputs, fn, invalidation)\` and a listener cell \`ss_listen(value, name, invalidation)\`. Until 2026-11-19 every cell was a call of \`ss.cell\`, which kept a result per cell and skipped the body on equal inputs, and until 2026-11-20 every cell took one object \`ss\` holding the whole runtime; all three are gone.

A rejected cell does not run: its definition only raises the checker's messages.`
// %%
readme_editing = md`## Editing

\`ss_registration\` registers the language on the plugin point \`cell_languages\`. Only this notebook's copy of \`@tomlarkworthy/cell-map\` has that plugin point; this notebook's copies of \`@tomlarkworthy/editor-5\` and \`@tomlarkworthy/visualizer\` read it.

The visualizer shows a cell's value with the normal Inspector. An action, a function, a listener, an events cell, a type and an element are drawn by \`ss_language.inspect\` instead: an element is mounted, the others are one inspector line such as \`bump = ƒ action()\`. An element positioned with \`position:absolute\` against a parent it has not got yet, such as Breakout's \`bricksView\`, is a line too, because mounted alone it has no box and covers the cells after it.

For a cell whose variables carry the marker, the editor shows the typed source, and its header line shows the inferred type, as \`doubled : number\`. It reports the checker's diagnostics as you type. What the edit does to other cells is shown on its first line: the cells it breaks, blocks or repairs, and after Shift-Enter the cells it broke, blocked or repaired.

Shift-Enter stores the edit whatever the checker says, unless it names no cell. An edit that takes another cell's name is stored under \`<name> (2)\` and rejected (S1.6). A cell that is not \`ok\` compiles to a definition that raises the checker's messages, with its typed source kept in the marker comment. A stored edit compiles again any other cell whose compiled form it changes. \`ss_lifecycle\` does the same for a change made outside the editor, such as a deleted cell.`
// %%
readme_limits = md`## Limits

- The editor and visualizer hooks need the \`cell_languages\` plugin point, which only this notebook's copies of \`@tomlarkworthy/cell-map\`, \`@tomlarkworthy/editor-5\` and \`@tomlarkworthy/visualizer\` have. Running these cells with other copies was not tried.
- A cell that does not parse is stored only if its text starts with \`const <name>\`, \`let <name>\` or \`function <name>\` (after comments, and with or without \`export\`); otherwise there is no name to store it under.
- A module holds one source file's worth of cells. Unchecked shell cells and trusted foreign declarations, which the checker can read, are not supported here.
- The renderer's event decoding and \`mount\` of the runtime module are outside the checked language.
- Publishing these modules to ObservableHQ was not tried.`
// %%
readme_api = ss_highlightCode(md`## API

\`\`\`
soundscript.checkSources({ cells, tsx, outside })  // the checker: per cell {name, status, errors, unsupported, value (its type)}
soundscript.check(source, tsx = true, outside)  // checkSources, remembered for the last 16 sources; .facts per cell (not enumerable)
soundscript.compileCell(source, tsx, context, name?)  // one cell's source -> [{name, inputs, definition}]; context: ss_context(module texts); name: the variable's own name, which wins over the declared one
soundscript.decompileVariable(definition)       // a compiled definition -> the cell's source, or null
soundscript.compiler(() => source)              // the value of ss_compile: compile(...) for the cells of that source
soundscript.running(handles?)                   // listeners attached on the page (on these handles only, if given)
soundscript.pulling(handles?)                   // events cells whose generator is being pulled (of these handles only, if given)
soundscript.isEvents(value)                     // whether a value is an events cell's handle
soundscript.release(value)                      // a deleted variable's listener ends, or its events stop
soundscript.compiledKind(definition)             // the kind of a compiled definition (plain, apply, ref, events, listen or rejected), or null
ss_moduleCells(module)                 // a module's SoundScript cells: [{key, text, variable}]
ss_source(module)                      // those cells' source, joined in runtime order
ss_outside(module)                     // the module's cells in other languages: [{name, view?}]
ss_check(module)                       // checkSources over ss_source(module), with ss_outside(module)
ss_roundtrip(module)                   // decompile and recompile every cell; throws on a difference
ss_language                            // the object registered on cell_languages; .inspect draws a value;
                                       // .hosts(module), .toBuiltin(source, …), .fromBuiltin(source, …) serve the editor's language picker
ss_instance(module, invalidation)      // a second, unseen copy of module's SoundScript cells, for tests
ss_highlight(text), ss_highlightCode(node)  // TypeScript colouring as spans; an md cell's code blocks coloured
cellListing(module, invalidation, {from, to})  // a module's cells in any registered language, as one listing
ss_tests_on                            // pending until "run the tests" is on; test cells take it as an input
\`\`\``)
// %%
ss_now = () => performance.now()
// %%
ss_random = Math.random
// %%
ss_log = (...args) => console.log(...args)
// %%
ss_fetch = globalThis.fetch.bind(globalThis)
// %%
viewof ss_module = thisModule()
// %%
ss_runtimeModule = ss_module.value("module @tomlarkworthy/soundscript-runtime")
// %%
ss_keyOf = (name) => soundscript.keyOfVariable(name)
// %%
ss_isSs = (v) => {
  // a SoundScript variable: its definition carries the language marker, or it is the value variable of a
  // SoundScript state cell (Observable's own Generators.input of the handle, which holds no source)
  if (typeof v?._definition !== "function") return false;
  const def = String(v._definition);
  if (soundscript.langOf(def) === "ss") return true;
  const handle = def === soundscript.STATE_VALUE && typeof v._name === "string" ? v._module?._scope?.get(`viewof ${v._name}`) : null;
  return typeof handle?._definition === "function" && soundscript.langOf(String(handle._definition)) === "ss";
}
// %%
ss_moduleCells = (module) => {
  // runtime order, one entry per cell: a state cell's two variables give one
  const out = [], seen = new Set();
  for (const v of runtime._variables) {
    if (v._module !== module || typeof v._name !== "string" || typeof v._definition !== "function") continue;
    if (!ss_isSs(v)) continue;
    let text = soundscript.decompileVariable(String(v._definition));
    if (text === null) continue;
    const key = ss_keyOf(v._name);
    // a compiled definition copied under another name (bump_copy) decompiles to the original's name;
    // the variable's own name wins, so recompiling it never defines a second bump
    if (!key.startsWith("type ") && !soundscript.isDuplicateKey(key)) {
      const head = soundscript.declaredNameAt(text);
      if (head && head.name !== key) text = text.slice(0, head.start) + key + text.slice(head.end);
    }
    if (seen.has(key)) continue;
    seen.add(key);
    out.push({ key, text, variable: v });
  }
  // a name declared again (stored as "<name> (2)", ...) comes after every other cell, so the checker
  // sees it as the later declaration, and the cell with the plain name keeps it
  const dup = out.filter((c) => soundscript.isDuplicateKey(c.key)).sort((a, b) => (a.key < b.key ? -1 : 1));
  return dup.length ? [...out.filter((c) => !soundscript.isDuplicateKey(c.key)), ...dup] : out;
}
// %%
ss_outside = (module) => {
  // the module's cells in other languages (Observable JavaScript, raw, imports), by name, sorted: a
  // SoundScript cell may take one through an annotated parameter, checked when its value crosses.
  // view: the module also has viewof <name> (a view, or an imported state cell's handle), so the cell can
  // be taken as State.
  const names = new Map();
  for (const v of runtime._variables) {
    if (v._module !== module || typeof v._name !== "string" || typeof v._definition !== "function") continue;
    if (ss_isSs(v)) continue;
    const view = v._name.startsWith("viewof ");
    const name = view ? v._name.slice(7) : v._name;
    if (!/^[\w$]+$/.test(name) || soundscript.RUNTIME_CELLS.some((n) => soundscript.INPUTS[n] === name)) continue;
    names.set(name, view || !!names.get(name));
  }
  return [...names].sort(([a], [b]) => (a < b ? -1 : 1)).map(([name, view]) => (view ? { name, view } : { name }));
}
// %%
ss_check = (module) => {
  // one check of the module; a cell that does not parse is checked as a stand-in (soundscript.checkCells)
  const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
  const { result } = soundscript.checkCells(cells.map((c) => c.text), true, ss_outside(module));
  return { cells, source: cells.map((c) => c.text).join("\n\n"), result, states: soundscript.cellStates(result) };
}
// %%
ss_context = (texts, module) => {
  // the compile context of a module's cells, from one (remembered) check of the whole module: which
  // cells are generators, which are taken as Events, which the checker accepts (only those run; any
  // other cell compiles to a definition that raises the checker's messages); the runtime module takes its own cells
  return { ...soundscript.contextFromCheck(soundscript.checkCells(texts, true, module ? ss_outside(module) : null).result), inputs: soundscript.inputsIn(!!module && module === ss_runtimeModule) };
}
// %%
ss_source = (module) => soundscript.joinCells(ss_moduleCells(module).map((c) => c.text))
// %%
ss_roundtrip = (module) => {
  let n = 0;
  const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
  const ctx = ss_context(cells.map((c) => c.text), module);
  for (const c of cells) {
    for (const d of soundscript.compileCell(c.text, true, ctx, c.key)) {
      const v = module._scope.get(d.name);
      if (!v) throw new Error(`${d.name}: no variable`);
      if (String(v._definition) !== d.definition) throw new Error(`${d.name}: the definition does not recompile to itself`);
      if (JSON.stringify(v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)) !== JSON.stringify(d.inputs)) throw new Error(`${d.name}: inputs ${v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)} vs ${d.inputs}`);
      n++;
    }
  }
  return n;
}
// %%
ss_instances = new WeakSet()
// %%
ss_deleted = {
  // A deleted variable's listener ends, or its events stop, once: the runtime does not resolve a
  // deleted variable's invalidation, and one deletion reaches both apply and onCodeChange.
  const done = new WeakSet();
  return (v) => { if (done.has(v)) return; done.add(v); soundscript.release(v._value); };
}
// %%
ss_instance = async (module, invalidation) => {
  // A second copy of module's SoundScript cells in a module of its own, so a test drives its own state cells
  // and listeners, not the ones on the page. Inputs its cells do not define (ss, ss_now, ...) are read from
  // module. Deleted on invalidation.
  const vars = [...runtime._variables].filter((v) => v._module === module && typeof v._name === "string" && ss_isSs(v));
  const names = new Set(vars.map((v) => v._name));
  // Generators, like invalidation, is the runtime's own, so the instance module resolves it itself
  const outside = new Set(vars.flatMap((v) => v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)).filter((n) => !names.has(n) && n !== "invalidation" && n !== "@variable" && n !== "Generators"));
  const fns = await realize(vars.map((v) => String(v._definition)), runtime);
  const inst = runtime.module();
  ss_instances.add(inst);
  for (const n of outside) inst.define(n, [], () => module.value(n));
  const made = vars.map((v, i) => inst.define(v._name, v._inputs.map((x) => x._name), fns[i]));
  const cancels = made.map((v) => observe(v, {}));
  invalidation.then(() => { cancels.forEach((c) => c()); for (const v of [...runtime._variables]) if (v._module === inst) { ss_deleted(v); v.delete(); } });
  return inst;
}
// %%
ss_lifecycle = {
  // Edits made outside apply (the editor's delete button, another tool) reach a module through
  // onCodeChange, which diffs snapshots of the runtime's variables. A variable added and deleted
  // between two snapshots produces no event of its own, so on any SoundScript change the whole
  // module is recompiled to its fixpoint (settle), and listeners and events that no variable holds
  // any more are stopped (sweep). The runtime does not resolve a deleted variable's invalidation.
  const isSs = ss_isSs;
  let scheduled = false;
  const touched = new Set();
  const off = onCodeChange(({ variable, previous }) => {
    const module = variable?._module ?? previous?._module;
    // a cell in another language added, deleted or renamed changes what its SoundScript readers check against
    const outsideNamed = !isSs(variable) && !isSs(previous) && variable?._name !== previous?._name && ss_language.hosts(module) && !ss_instances.has(module);
    if (outsideNamed) touched.add(module);
    else if (!isSs(variable) && !isSs(previous)) return;
    if (variable === null && !outsideNamed) ss_deleted(previous.variable);
    if (ss_language.hosts(module) && !ss_instances.has(module)) touched.add(module);
    if (scheduled) return;
    scheduled = true;
    queueMicrotask(() => {
      scheduled = false;
      soundscript.sweep(new Set([...runtime._variables].map((x) => x._value)));
      soundscript.listenerOrderChanged();
      for (const m of touched) ss_language.settle(m).catch((e) => console.error(e));
      touched.clear();
    });
  });
  // where a listener's cell is, for the order listeners of one events cell run in: its module's name
  // and its place among that module's variables, which is the order the module is saved in
  const unnamed = new WeakMap();
  const nameOf = (m) => { for (const [n, x] of runtime.mains ?? []) if (x === m) return n; if (!unnamed.has(m)) unnamed.set(m, `~${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8)}`); return unnamed.get(m); };
  soundscript.setListenerOrder((values) => {
    const want = new Set(values), at = new Map(), seen = new Map();
    for (const v of runtime._variables) {
      const n = (seen.get(v._module) ?? 0) + 1;
      seen.set(v._module, n);
      if (want.has(v._value) && !at.has(v._value)) at.set(v._value, [v._module, n]);
    }
    return values.map((x) => { const p = at.get(x); return p ? [nameOf(p[0]), p[1]] : null; });
  });
  // the name an error report gives an action: the SoundScript cell whose value it is
  soundscript.actionNamer.of = (a) => { for (const v of runtime._variables) if (v._value === a && isSs(v)) return ss_keyOf(v._name); return null; };
  invalidation.then(() => { off(); soundscript.setListenerOrder(null); soundscript.actionNamer.of = null; });
  return "a change outside apply recompiles its module and stops listeners and events no variable holds";
}
// %%
ss_language = {
  const tsx = true;
  const isSs = ss_isSs;
  const keyOf = ss_keyOf;
  const moduleOf = (variables, cell) => variables.find((v) => v?._module)?._module ?? cell?.module?.module;
  const family = (module, key) => (key.startsWith("type ") ? [soundscript.variableName(key)] : [soundscript.variableName(key), soundscript.handleName(key)]).map((n) => module?._scope?.get(n)).filter(isSs);
  const ownKey = (variables) => { const v = variables.find(isSs); return v ? keyOf(v._name) : null; };
  const sourceOf = (v) => soundscript.decompileVariable(String(v._definition));

  const decompile = async (variables) => {
    for (const v of variables) if (isSs(v)) { const s = sourceOf(v); if (s !== null) return s; }
    // a state cell's value variable holds no source; its handle variable does
    const key = ownKey(variables);
    for (const v of family(moduleOf(variables), key)) { const s = sourceOf(v); if (s !== null) return s; }
    throw new Error(`no SoundScript source for ${key}`);
  };

  // what storing an edit does to the other cells: those ok now that would not be, and the reverse
  const plural = (n) => `${n} cell${n === 1 ? "" : "s"}`;
  // (breaks: ok before, rejected after; blocks: ok before, blocked after; repairs: not ok before, ok after)
  const effectOf = (before, after) => {
    const was = (n, f) => before.has(n) && f(before.get(n).state);
    const breaks = [...after].filter(([n, x]) => x.state === "rejected" && was(n, (s) => s === "ok")).map(([n]) => n);
    const blocks = [...after].filter(([n, x]) => x.state === "blocked" && was(n, (s) => s === "ok")).map(([n]) => n);
    const repairs = [...after].filter(([n, x]) => x.state === "ok" && was(n, (s) => s !== "ok")).map(([n]) => n);
    return { breaks, blocks, repairs };
  };
  const sayEffect = ({ breaks, blocks, repairs }, done) => {
    const parts = [];
    if (breaks.length) parts.push(`${done ? "broke" : "breaks"} ${plural(breaks.length)}: ${breaks.join(", ")}`);
    if (blocks.length) parts.push(`${done ? "blocked" : "blocks"} ${plural(blocks.length)}: ${blocks.join(", ")}`);
    if (repairs.length) parts.push(`${done ? "repaired" : "repairs"} ${plural(repairs.length)}: ${repairs.join(", ")}`);
    return parts.length ? `${done ? "this edit" : "applying this"} ${parts.join("; ")}` : "";
  };
  // the last stored edit's effect, per module and cell, shown on that cell while its text is unchanged
  const lastEffect = new WeakMap();

  // {ok (the edited cell checks), store (Shift-Enter stores it), problems: [{line, rule, msg}] with lines
  // relative to source, effect, defs, texts, state}. Every edit is stored except one that names no cell;
  // one that takes the name of another cell is stored as "<name> (2)" and rejected.
  const check = (source, variables = [], cell) => {
    const module = moduleOf(variables, cell);
    const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
    const texts = cells.map((c) => c.text);
    const oldKey = ownKey(variables);
    let at = cells.findIndex((c) => c.key === oldKey);
    if (at < 0) { texts.push(source); at = texts.length - 1; } else texts[at] = source;
    // an edit that takes the name of another cell is stored as "<name> (2)" and rejected; it goes after
    // the other cells, so the checker sees it as the later declaration
    const named = soundscript.declaredName(source);
    const takesCell = !!named && named !== oldKey && cells.some((c) => c.key === named);
    if (takesCell && at !== texts.length - 1) { texts.splice(at, 1); texts.push(source); at = texts.length - 1; }
    const there0 = named && named !== oldKey ? module?._scope?.get(named) : null;
    const takesOther = !takesCell && !!there0 && !isSs(there0) && !variables.includes(there0);
    // one check of the module as edited gives the verdicts, the compile context and the cell facts
    let after = null, checkError = null;
    const outside = module ? ss_outside(module).filter((o) => !(takesOther && o.name === named)) : null;
    try { after = soundscript.checkCells(texts, true, outside).result; } catch (e) { checkError = e; }
    if (!after) return { ok: false, store: false, problems: [{ line: 1, rule: "check", msg: `${checkError.message}; a cell that does not parse is stored only when it starts with const, let or function <name>` }] };
    let defs, ctx = { ...soundscript.contextFromCheck(after), inputs: soundscript.inputsIn(!!module && module === ss_runtimeModule) }, hint = oldKey;
    if (takesCell && soundscript.isDuplicateKey(after.cells.at(-1)?.name)) hint = after.cells.at(-1).name;
    if (takesOther) {
      let k = 2;
      while (module._scope.has(soundscript.variableName(`${named} (${k})`))) k++;
      hint = `${named} (${k})`;
      ctx = { ...ctx, why: new Map([...(ctx.why ?? []), [hint, [`[duplicate-cell] ${named} is already defined in this module, in another language`]]]) };
    }
    try { defs = soundscript.compileCell(source, tsx, ctx, hint); }
    catch (e) { return { ok: false, store: false, problems: [{ line: e.loc?.line ?? 1, rule: "compile", msg: e.message }] }; }
    const key = keyOf(defs.at(-1).name);
    const own = new Set([...variables, ...(oldKey ? family(module, oldKey) : [])]);
    const problems = [];
    let store = true;
    for (const d of defs) {
      const there = module?._scope?.get(d.name);
      if (there && !own.has(there)) { store = false; problems.push({ line: 1, rule: "duplicate-cell", msg: `${d.name} is already defined in this module, so this edit is not stored` }); }
    }
    const start = texts.slice(0, at).reduce((n, t) => n + t.split("\n").length + 1, 0);
    const end = start + source.split("\n").length;
    const rel = (e) => ({ ...e, line: Math.max(1, e.line - start) });
    const parseMsg = after.unparsed?.get(key);
    if (parseMsg !== undefined) problems.push({ line: Number(/\((\d+):\d+\)/.exec(parseMsg)?.[1] ?? 1), rule: "parse", msg: parseMsg });
    for (const e of after.module) if (e.line > start && e.line <= end) problems.push(rel(e));
    const mine = parseMsg === undefined ? after.cells.find((c) => c.name === key) : null;
    if (takesOther) problems.push({ line: 1, rule: "duplicate-cell", msg: `${named} is already defined in this module, in another language` });
    if (mine) {
      for (const e of mine.errors) problems.push(rel(e));
      for (const u of mine.unsupported) problems.push({ ...rel(u), rule: "unsupported" });
    }
    const statesAfter = soundscript.cellStates(after);
    let statesBefore = new Map();
    try { statesBefore = soundscript.cellStates(soundscript.checkCells(cells.map((c) => c.text), true, outside).result); } catch {}
    const state = statesAfter.get(key) ?? { state: "rejected", why: [], blockedBy: [] };
    if (state.state === "blocked") problems.push({ line: 1, rule: "blocked", msg: `blocked by ${state.blockedBy.join(", ")}: it does not run until ${state.blockedBy.length > 1 ? "they are" : "that is"} ok` });
    const effect = sayEffect(effectOf(statesBefore, statesAfter), false);
    return { ok: problems.length === 0 && state.state === "ok", store, problems, effect, statesBefore, statesAfter, defs, key, texts, ctx, hint, state: state.state, status: mine?.status ?? (parseMsg !== undefined ? "rejected" : null), type: mine?.value ?? null };
  };

  // the annotation the current value of a cell in another language suggests; the value is read, never computed
  const annotationIn = (module, name) => {
    const v = module?._scope?.get(name);
    return v && !v._error ? soundscript.annotationOf(v._value) : null;
  };
  // a name the body reads that is a cell of the module: the parameter that takes it. A SoundScript cell is
  // taken bare (its type is inferred); one in another language with its value's annotation, else unknown (S11.3)
  const paramFix = (p, module) => {
    const m = p.rule === "cell-by-name" ? /^cell ([\w$]+) referenced by name/.exec(p.msg) : p.rule === "free-name" ? /^free name ([\w$]+)$/.exec(p.msg) : null;
    if (!m) return null;
    const name = m[1];
    let ann = null;
    if (p.rule === "free-name") {
      if (!module || !ss_outside(module).some((o) => o.name === name)) return null;
      ann = annotationIn(module, name) ?? "unknown";
    }
    return { name, ann };
  };
  const lint = (source, variables = [], cell) => {
    const starts = [0];
    for (let i = 0; i < source.length; i++) if (source[i] === "\n") starts.push(i + 1);
    const r = check(source, variables, cell);
    const module = moduleOf(variables, cell);
    const diags = r.problems.map((p) => {
      const l = Math.min(Math.max(p.line, 1), starts.length) - 1;
      const to = l + 1 < starts.length ? starts[l + 1] - 1 : source.length;
      const d = { from: starts[l], to: Math.max(to, starts[l]), severity: "error", message: `[${p.rule}] ${p.msg}` };
      const fix = paramFix(p, module);
      if (fix && soundscript.addParameter(source, fix.name, fix.ann)) {
        // the diagnostic covers the name where it is read on that line
        const toks = soundscript.tokensOf(source.slice(d.from, d.to));
        const hit = toks.find((t, i) => t.label === "name" && t.value === fix.name && toks[i - 1]?.label !== ".");
        if (hit) { d.to = d.from + hit.end; d.from += hit.start; }
        d.actions = [{ name: `Add ${fix.ann ? `${fix.name}: ${fix.ann}` : fix.name} as a parameter`, apply: (view) => {
          const e = soundscript.addParameter(view.state.doc.toString(), fix.name, fix.ann);
          if (e) view.dispatch({ changes: e });
        } }];
      }
      return d;
    });
    // what applying would do to the other cells, or, once applied, what it did
    const done = r.key ? lastEffect.get(moduleOf(variables, cell))?.get(r.key) : null;
    const say = r.effect || (done && done.text === source ? done.msg : "");
    if (say) diags.push({ from: 0, to: Math.min(starts[1] ? starts[1] - 1 : source.length, source.length), severity: "info", message: say });
    // `export` is still accepted, so a stored cell round-trips; the form is without it
    const [t0, t1] = soundscript.tokensOf(source, 2);
    if (t0?.label === "export" && t1 && ["const", "let", "function", "async", "type", "interface"].includes(String(t1.value))) {
      const from = t0.start, to = t1.start;
      diags.push({ from, to, severity: "hint", message: "export is not needed", actions: [{ name: "Remove export", apply: (view, f, t) => view.dispatch({ changes: { from: f, to: t } }) }] });
    }
    return diags;
  };

  // Replaces the variables in old with defs; new variables go after anchor.
  // With a transaction tx {made, doomed}, new variables are recorded and old ones are only marked, so
  // the caller can delete them on commit or undo everything.
  // batches [{defs, old, anchor}]: every definition is realized first, then all are defined in one
  // synchronous step, so the runtime never computes a cell between two of them (a reader the edit
  // rejects would otherwise run once on the edited input). afterFirst runs after the first batch.
  // the runtime cells the definitions take that module lacks are imported first, as the build imports them (freeze as ss_freeze)
  const RUNTIME = new Map(soundscript.RUNTIME_CELLS.map((n) => [soundscript.INPUTS[n], n])), MV = "module @tomlarkworthy/soundscript-runtime";
  const importInputs = async (module, defs, tx) => {
    const want = [...new Set(defs.flatMap((d) => d.inputs))].filter((i) => RUNTIME.has(i) && !module._scope.has(i));
    if (!want.length) return;
    const fns = await realize(want.map((i) => `(_, v) => v.import(${JSON.stringify(RUNTIME.get(i))}, ${JSON.stringify(i)}, _)`), runtime);
    if (!module._scope.has(MV)) tx?.made.push(module.variable().define(MV, [], ss_module._scope.get(MV)._definition));
    tx?.made.push(...want.map((i, k) => module.variable().define(i, [MV, "@variable"], fns[k])));
  };
  const defineAll = async (module, batches, tx = null, afterFirst = null) => {
    await importInputs(module, batches.flatMap((b) => b.defs), tx);
    const all = await realize(batches.flatMap((b) => b.defs.map((d) => d.definition)), runtime);
    let k = 0;
    return batches.map((b, i) => {
      const out = defineNow(module, b.defs, b.old, b.anchor, tx, all.slice(k, (k += b.defs.length)));
      if (i === 0) afterFirst?.();
      return out;
    });
  };
  const define = async (module, defs, old, anchor, tx = null) => (await defineAll(module, [{ defs, old, anchor }], tx))[0];
  const defineNow = (module, defs, old, anchor, tx, fns) => {
    const fresh = [];
    const next = defs.map((d, i) => {
      let v = module._scope.get(d.name);
      if (!v || !old.has(v)) {
        v = module.variable({});
        v.pid = "_" + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 9);
        fresh.push(v);
        tx?.made.push(v);
      }
      v.define(d.name, d.inputs, fns[i]);
      return v;
    });
    // placed before the old variables go, since a deleted anchor has no position
    if (anchor && fresh.length) {
      let at = [...runtime._variables].indexOf(anchor) + 1;
      for (const v of fresh) repositionSetElement(runtime._variables, v, at++);
    }
    const drop = (v) => { ss_deleted(v); v.delete(); };
    for (const v of old) if (!next.includes(v)) tx ? tx.doomed.push(v) : drop(v);
    return next;
  };
  const same = (vs, defs) => vs.length === defs.length && defs.every((d) => {
    const v = vs.find((x) => x._name === d.name);
    return v && String(v._definition) === d.definition && JSON.stringify(v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)) === JSON.stringify(d.inputs);
  });

  // Stores the edit whatever its verdict (not stored, returning undefined: no cell name; another cell's
  // name is stored as "<name> (2)"). A cell the checker does not accept compiles to a definition that raises its messages.
  // Every other cell whose compiled form the edit changes is compiled again too: one that becomes, or
  // stops being, accepted; a generator that became, or stopped being, taken as Events.
  const applyNow = async (source, variables = [], cell) => {
    const r = check(source, variables, cell);
    if (!r.store) return undefined;
    const module = moduleOf(variables, cell);
    const oldKey = ownKey(variables);
    // a Notebook Kit cell converted to SoundScript also takes its shadow variables (display) with it
    const old = new Set([...variables.flatMap((v) => [v, ...(v._shadow?.values() ?? [])]), ...(oldKey ? family(module, oldKey) : [])]);
    const order = [...runtime._variables];
    const anchor = [...old].sort((a, b) => order.indexOf(a) - order.indexOf(b)).at(-1) ?? cell?.variables?.at(-1);
    // every other cell whose compiled form the edit changes is compiled before anything is defined
    const ctx = ss_context(r.texts, module);
    const plan = [];
    for (const c of ss_moduleCells(module)) {
      if (c.key === r.key || c.key === oldKey) continue;
      const defs = soundscript.compileCell(c.text, tsx, ctx, c.key);
      const fam = family(module, c.key);
      if (!same(fam, defs)) plan.push({ defs, fam });
    }
    // then all of it is defined; if any step throws, every variable touched gets its old definition back
    const touchedVars = new Set([...old, ...plan.flatMap((p) => p.fam)]);
    const saved = [...touchedVars].map((v) => ({ v, name: v._name, inputs: v._inputs.map((i) => i._name), definition: v._definition }));
    const tx = { made: [], doomed: [] };
    // what the edit does is known before anything is defined; it is recorded now, so a lint that runs while
    // the cells are being defined (it sees no change left to make) still says what the edit did
    const msg = sayEffect(effectOf(r.statesBefore, r.statesAfter), true);
    if (!lastEffect.has(module)) lastEffect.set(module, new Map());
    lastEffect.get(module).set(r.key, { text: source, msg });
    let next;
    try {
      [next] = await defineAll(module, [{ defs: r.defs, old, anchor }, ...plan.map((p) => ({ defs: p.defs, old: new Set(p.fam), anchor: p.fam.at(-1) }))], tx, () => {
        if (faults.afterEditDefine === module) throw new Error("injected fault after the edited cell was defined");
      });
    } catch (e) {
      lastEffect.get(module).delete(r.key);
      for (const v of tx.made) v.delete();
      for (const s of saved) s.v.define(s.name, s.inputs, s.definition);
      throw e;
    }
    for (const v of new Set(tx.doomed)) { ss_deleted(v); v.delete(); }
    // a reused Kit head no longer has shadows; theirs were deleted with the rest of old
    for (const v of next) v._shadow?.clear?.();
    variables.splice(0, variables.length, ...next);
    const stored = await decompile(next);
    lastEffect.get(module).set(r.key, { text: stored, msg });
    return stored;
  };
  // test hook: set afterEditDefine to a module, and an apply there fails after defining the edited cell
  const faults = { afterEditDefine: null };
  // compiles again every cell of module (but skip) whose form the rest of the module changed
  const recompileNow = async (module, skip) => {
    const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
    const ctx = ss_context(cells.map((c) => c.text), module);
    const batches = [];
    for (const c of cells) {
      if (c.key === skip) continue;
      const defs = soundscript.compileCell(c.text, tsx, ctx, c.key);
      const fam = family(module, c.key);
      if (!same(fam, defs)) batches.push({ defs, old: new Set(fam), anchor: fam.at(-1) });
    }
    if (batches.length) await defineAll(module, batches);
    return batches.length;
  };

  // completion at pos in source, with the module's other cells as context: {from, to, options, mode}
  const complete = (source, pos, variables = [], cell) => {
    const module = moduleOf(variables, cell);
    const cells = ss_moduleCells(module);
    const texts = cells.map((c) => c.text);
    const at0 = cells.findIndex((c) => c.key === ownKey(variables));
    const at = at0 < 0 ? texts.length : at0;
    texts[at] = source;
    return soundscript.completionsAt(texts, at, pos, tsx, module ? ss_outside(module) : null, module ? (n) => annotationIn(module, n) : null);
  };
  // the editor's header: the cell's parameters as inputs (not ss or a hidden invalidation), named outputs
  const header = (variables) => {
    const v = variables.find((x) => isSs(x) && soundscript.decompileVariable(String(x._definition)) !== null);
    if (!v) return null;
    const text = soundscript.decompileVariable(String(v._definition));
    const params = new Set(soundscript.paramsOf(text) ?? []);
    const own = new Set(variables);
    const inputs = [...new Set(variables.flatMap((x) => x._inputs))].filter((i) => !own.has(i) && params.has(String(i._name).replace(/^viewof /, "")));
    const outputs = [...new Set(variables.flatMap((x) => [...x._outputs]))].filter((o) => !own.has(o) && typeof o._name === "string" && o._name);
    const name = keyOf(v._name);
    return { inputs, outputs, name, type: name.startsWith("type ") ? null : typesOf(v._module).get(name) ?? null };
  };

  // the checker's value type of each cell of a module, checked again only when one of its definitions changes
  const typeCache = new WeakMap();
  const typesOf = (module) => {
    if (!module) return new Map();
    const defs = [];
    for (const v of runtime._variables) if (v._module === module && isSs(v)) defs.push(v._definition);
    const hit = typeCache.get(module);
    if (hit && hit.defs.length === defs.length && hit.defs.every((d, i) => d === defs[i])) return hit.types;
    let types = new Map();
    try { types = new Map(ss_check(module).result.cells.map((c) => [c.name, c.value])); } catch {}
    typeCache.set(module, { defs, types });
    return types;
  };

  // How the visualizer shows a value: only the kinds the normal Inspector cannot read are drawn here, as
  // an inspector line (name = …) or, for an element, the element; null leaves the value to the Inspector.
  // The kind comes from the checker's type, not from the value's shape.
  const line = (name, text) => {
    const el = document.createElement("span");
    el.className = text.startsWith("ƒ") ? "observablehq--function observablehq--inspect" : "observablehq--inspect";
    const cellname = document.createElement("span");
    cellname.className = "observablehq--cellname";
    cellname.textContent = `${name} = `;
    const kw = document.createElement("span");
    kw.className = "observablehq--keyword";
    el.append(cellname);
    if (text.startsWith("ƒ")) { kw.textContent = "ƒ"; el.append(kw, text.slice(1)); } else el.append(text);
    return el;
  };
  const inspect = (variable, value, root, { pending = false } = {}) => {
    if (!isSs(variable) || typeof variable._name !== "string") return null;
    const key = keyOf(variable._name);
    // a type cell has no value, so it is drawn while pending; every other cell waits for its value
    if (pending && !key.startsWith("type ")) return null;
    // a state cell is drawn as Observable draws a viewof cell, by its handle variable: its value, as the normal
    // Inspector shows it, drawn again on each commit (the handle's input event)
    if (variable._name.startsWith("viewof ") && value instanceof EventTarget && "value" in value) {
      const el = document.createElement("div"), shown = new Inspector(el);
      root.__ssHandle?.();
      const draw = () => shown.fulfilled(value.value, key);
      value.addEventListener("input", draw);
      root.__ssHandle = () => value.removeEventListener("input", draw);
      draw();
      return el;
    }
    const def = String(variable._definition);
    if (key.startsWith("type ")) {
      const text = sourceOf(variable);
      return text === null ? null : line(key, text.replace(/^[\s\S]*?\btype\s+[\w$]+(?:<[^=]*>)?\s*=\s*/, "").replace(/;\s*$/, ""));
    }
    const type = typesOf(variable._module).get(key);
    if (!type) return null;
    if (soundscript.compiledKind(def)?.kind === "events") return line(key, `events Events<${type}>`);
    if (type === "Elem" && value && typeof value === "object" && "tag" in value) {
      // an element placed by position:absolute against a parent it has not got yet (Breakout's
      // bricksView) has no box of its own; mounted alone it would cover the cells after it
      const pos = (e) => /position\s*:\s*(absolute|relative|fixed)/.exec(String(e?.props?.style ?? ""))?.[1];
      const placed = (e) => pos(e) === "absolute" || (!pos(e) && (e?.children ?? []).some((c) => c && typeof c === "object" && placed(c)));
      if (placed(value)) return line(key, `<${value.tag || "fragment"}> element, positioned by its parent`);
      const el = soundscript.mount(value, root.__ssView ?? null);
      el.classList?.add("ss-view");
      root.__ssView = el;
      return el;
    }
    if (type === "Listener") {
      const text = sourceOf(family(variable._module, key)[0] ?? variable) ?? "";
      const pairs = [...text.matchAll(/\bon\(\s*([\w$]+)\s*,\s*([\w$]+)\s*\)/g)].map((m) => `${m[1]} → ${m[2]}`);
      return line(key, `listener ${pairs.join(" | ") || "?"}`);
    }
    if (typeof value !== "function") return null;
    const action = /^Action<\[(.*)\]>$/.exec(type);
    if (action) return line(key, `ƒ action(${action[1]})`);
    if (type.startsWith("(")) return line(key, `ƒ ${type}`);
    return null;
  };

  // typed text is SoundScript when its module hosts SoundScript cells, and it starts as a cell or a type does; the
  // editor takes the claim only when the built-in parser rejects the text
  const claimsSource = (source, cell) => {
    const module = cell?.module?.module;
    const [t0, t1] = soundscript.tokensOf(source, 2);
    const first = t0?.label === "export" ? t1 : t0;
    return hosts(module) && !!first && ["const", "let", "function", "async", "type", "interface"].includes(String(first.value));
  };

  // a module can hold SoundScript cells when it is the runtime module or imports rejected as ss_rejected (what any of
  // its cells compiles to when the checker does not accept it), as the build makes every module with SoundScript cells
  const hosts = (module) => !!module && (module === ss_runtimeModule || module._scope.has(soundscript.INPUTS.rejected));
  // The editor's language picker. toBuiltin: the cell as Observable JavaScript cell text, exactly the text
  // Observable's compiler makes this cell's variables of, compiled in its module as apply would.
  const toBuiltin = (source, variables = [], cell, target = "ojs") => {
    if (target !== "ojs") return { reason: "a SoundScript cell compiles to Observable JavaScript, not Notebook Kit JavaScript" };
    const r = check(source, variables, cell);
    const parse = r.problems.find((p) => p.rule === "parse" || p.rule === "check" || p.rule === "compile");
    // the first line of the message; what follows it is about storing, and a pick stores nothing
    if (parse) return { reason: `the text does not parse: ${String(parse.msg).split(";")[0]}` };
    const dup = r.problems.find((p) => p.rule === "duplicate-cell");
    if (dup) return { reason: `${soundscript.declaredName(source) ?? "this name"} is already defined in this module` };
    return { text: soundscript.compileCellText(source, tsx, r.ctx, r.hint) };
  };
  // fromBuiltin: Observable JavaScript as SoundScript. compiled: the variables the standard compiler made of
  // source; a compiled SoundScript cell gives its own source back, any other cell is translated.
  const fromBuiltin = (source, variables = [], cell, { lang, compiled, expression } = {}) => {
    if (!hosts(moduleOf(variables, cell))) return { reason: `this module does not import rejected as ${soundscript.INPUTS.rejected} from @tomlarkworthy/soundscript-runtime, the mark of a module with SoundScript cells` };
    if (lang !== "ojs" || !compiled) return { reason: "only Observable JavaScript translates to SoundScript" };
    const vars = compiled.map((v) => ({ name: v.name ?? null, inputs: v.inputs ?? [], definition: String(v.definition) }));
    for (const v of vars) if (soundscript.langOf(v.definition) === "ss") { const s = soundscript.decompileVariable(v.definition); if (s !== null) return { text: s }; }
    return soundscript.fromObservableVariables(vars, { expression });
  };

  // Edits and recompiles run one at a time, so a recompile never reads a module another is halfway
  // through defining. settle(module) queues at most one pending recompile per module.
  let queue = Promise.resolve();
  const serial = (f) => { const r = queue.then(f); queue = r.catch(() => {}); return r; };
  const apply = (...a) => serial(() => applyNow(...a));
  const recompile = (module, skip) => serial(() => recompileNow(module, skip));
  const pending = new Set();
  const settle = (module) => {
    if (pending.has(module)) return queue;
    pending.add(module);
    return serial(() => { pending.delete(module); return recompileNow(module); });
  };
  return {
    id: "ss",
    label: "SoundScript",
    claimsSource,
    hosts,
    toBuiltin,
    fromBuiltin,
    decompile,
    check,
    lint,
    complete,
    header,
    inspect,
    apply,
    faults,
    recompile,
    settle,
    highlight: (text) => ss_highlight(text),
    extension: (codemirror) => codemirror.javascript({ typescript: true, jsx: true })
  };
}
// %%
ss_registration = {
  plugins.add("cell_languages", ss_language, { invalidation });
  return md`SoundScript is registered as the editor language \`${ss_language.id}\` (plugin \`cell_languages\`).`;
}
// %%
ss_highlight = {
  // TypeScript and JSX colouring with the editor's own parser, as spans with CodeMirror's tok-* classes
  const lang = codemirror.javascript({ typescript: true, jsx: true }).language;
  return (text) => {
    const out = [];
    let at = 0;
    lezerhighlight.highlightTree(lang.parser.parse(text), lezerhighlight.classHighlighter, (from, to, cls) => {
      if (from > at) out.push(text.slice(at, from));
      const span = document.createElement("span");
      span.className = cls;
      span.textContent = text.slice(from, to);
      out.push(span);
      at = to;
    });
    if (at < text.length) out.push(text.slice(at));
    return out;
  };
}
// %%
ss_highlightCode = (node) => {
  // colours an md cell's code blocks with ss_highlight; a fence without a language, so md fetches no highlighter
  for (const code of node.querySelectorAll("pre > code")) {
    code.classList.add("ss-hl");
    code.replaceChildren(...ss_highlight(code.textContent));
  }
  return node;
}
// %%
ss_hl_css = [
  // the editor's syntax colours, 30% toward the foreground: the light theme's own are 3.2 to 4.4:1 on the alt background
  [".tok-keyword, .tok-modifier, .tok-controlKeyword, .tok-operatorKeyword", "keyword"],
  [".tok-string, .tok-string2", "string"],
  [".tok-number, .tok-bool, .tok-atom, .tok-null", "literal"],
  [".tok-comment", "comment", "font-style: italic;"],
  [".tok-definition", "definition"],
  [".tok-typeName, .tok-className", "atom"],
  [".tok-propertyName", "variable"],
].map(([sel, c, extra = ""]) => `${sel.split(", ").map((x) => ".ss-hl " + x).join(", ")} { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--syntax-${c}) 70%, var(--theme-foreground)); ${extra} }`).join("\n")
// %%
ss_hl_style = htl.html`<style>${ss_hl_css}
.cell-listing { margin: 0; padding: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; border: 1px solid var(--theme-foreground-faint); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--theme-background-alt); }
</style>`
// %%
cellListing = {
  // a language registering makes a new cellListing, so every listing is drawn again
  cellLanguagesVersion;
  return (module, invalidation, { from = null, to = null } = {}) => {
  // a module's cells from cell from to cell to (all of them without), in any language registered on
  // cell_languages: each cell's source is its language's decompile, coloured by its highlight when it has one;
  // read again when the module's code changes. A cell of no registered language is left out.
  const pre = htl.html`<pre class="cell-listing ss-hl">`;
  const keyOf = (name) => soundscript.keyOfVariable(String(name).replace(/^(mutable|initial) /, ""));
  let shown = null, queued = false, round = 0;
  const draw = async () => {
    queued = false;
    const mine = ++round;
    const vars = [...runtime._variables].filter((v) => v._module === module && v._type === 1);
    const cells = (await cellMap(vars)).get(module) ?? [];
    const parts = [];
    for (const c of cells) {
      const lang = languageOf(c.variables, c);
      if (!lang?.decompile) continue;
      // a cell mid-redefinition may have no source yet; it is drawn on the next change
      let text = null;
      try { text = await lang.decompile(c.variables); } catch {}
      if (typeof text === "string") parts.push({ key: keyOf(c.name), lang, text });
    }
    if (mine !== round) return;
    const keys = parts.map((p) => p.key);
    const a = from === null ? 0 : keys.indexOf(from), b = to === null ? parts.length - 1 : keys.indexOf(to);
    const pick = parts.slice(Math.max(a, 0), b < 0 ? parts.length : b + 1);
    const text = pick.map((p) => p.text).join("\n\n");
    if (text === shown) return;
    shown = text;
    pre.replaceChildren(...pick.flatMap((p, i) => [...(i ? ["\n\n"] : []), ...(p.lang.highlight ? p.lang.highlight(p.text) : [p.text])]));
  };
  const off = onCodeChange(({ variable, previous }) => { if ((variable ?? previous)?._module === module && !queued) { queued = true; queueMicrotask(draw); } });
  draw();
  invalidation.then(off);
  return pre;
  };
}
// %%
style = htl.html`<style>
.ss-tests td, .ss-tests th { max-width: 28ch; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
.ss-example { padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--theme-foreground-faint); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--theme-background-alt); }
</style>`
// %%
readme_tests = md`## Tests

The tests run only when **run the tests** is on, so a page that is only read spends nothing on them. Each test takes \`ss_tests_on\`, which stays pending until then; a pending test has not passed. \`test_ss_ref_handle\` presses **bump** and **reset** on a copy of this module (\`ss_instance\`), so the counter on the page keeps its count.`
// %%
viewof ss_run_tests = Inputs.toggle({ label: "run the tests" })
// %%
ss_tests_on = ss_run_tests ? true : invalidation
// %%
test_ss_roundtrip = {
  ss_tests_on;
  const n = ss_roundtrip(ss_module);
  if (n < 5) throw new Error(`${n} SoundScript variables in this module; the example alone has 5 (tally is two)`);
  return `${n} variables recompile to the same text and inputs`;
}
// %%
test_ss_example_checks = {
  ss_tests_on;
  const { result } = ss_check(ss_module);
  const want = ["tally", "bump", "reset", "doubled"];
  const got = Object.fromEntries(want.map((n) => [n, result.cells.find((c) => c.name === n)?.status]));
  if (want.some((n) => got[n] !== "ok")) throw new Error(`verdicts ${JSON.stringify(got)}`);
  return `${want.join(", ")}: ok`;
}
// %%
test_ss_unchanged_source_checks = {
  ss_tests_on;
  const v = ss_module._scope.get("bump");
  const source = await ss_language.decompile([v]);
  const r = ss_language.check(source, [v]);
  if (!r.ok || r.problems.length) throw new Error(JSON.stringify(r.problems));
  return `bump: ok, type ${r.type}`;
}
// %%
test_ss_wrong_type_is_stored_and_rejected = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // an edit the checker rejects is stored; the cell then raises the checker's message instead of running
  let end;
  const done = new Promise((r) => (end = r));
  try {
    const inst = await ss_instance(ss_module, done);
    const original = await ss_language.decompile([inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    const source = original.replace("tally: State<number>", "tally: State<string>");
    if (source === original) throw new Error("bump has no tally: State<number> parameter to change");
    const r = ss_language.check(source, [inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    if (r.ok || !r.store || !r.problems.some((p) => p.rule === "inject-state")) throw new Error(`check: ${JSON.stringify(r.problems)}`);
    const lint = ss_language.lint(source, [inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    if (!lint.some((d) => d.severity === "error")) throw new Error(`lint: ${JSON.stringify(lint)}`);
    const stored = await ss_language.apply(source, [inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    if (stored !== source) throw new Error(`stored ${JSON.stringify(stored)}`);
    let threw = null;
    try { await inst.value("bump"); } catch (e) { threw = e; }
    if (!/^bump does not check: \[inject-state\]/.test(threw?.message ?? "")) throw new Error(`bump gave ${threw?.message ?? "a value"}`);
    await ss_language.apply(original, [inst._scope.get("bump")]);
    if (typeof (await inst.value("bump")) !== "function") throw new Error("bump did not come back after the repair");
    return `stored; bump raises "${threw.message.slice(0, 80)}"; repaired, it is an action again`;
  } finally { end(); }
}
// %%
test_ss_breaking_edit_names_its_cells = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // before an edit is stored, the editor says which cells it would break
  const v = ss_module._scope.get("tally");
  const original = await ss_language.decompile([v]);
  const source = original.replace("StateCell<number> => state(0)", 'StateCell<string> => state("0")');
  if (source === original) throw new Error("tally is not StateCell<number> => state(0)");
  const r = ss_language.check(source, [v]);
  // bump, reset and doubled take tally; a cell added later that reads doubled is blocked
  if (!r.store || !/^applying this breaks 3 cells: bump, reset, doubled(; blocks \d+ cells?: [\w, ]+)?$/.test(r.effect)) throw new Error(`effect ${JSON.stringify(r.effect)}`);
  const d = r.statesAfter.get("doubled");
  if (d.state !== "rejected" || !d.why.some((w) => w.includes("string is not assignable to number"))) throw new Error(`doubled ${JSON.stringify(d)}`);
  const back = ss_language.check(original, [v]);
  if (back.effect !== "") throw new Error(`the unchanged source reports ${JSON.stringify(back.effect)}`);
  return r.effect;
}
// %%
test_ss_copy_keeps_its_name = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // a definition copied under another name recompiles under the copy's own name, not the original's
  let end;
  const done = new Promise((r) => (end = r));
  try {
    const inst = await ss_instance(ss_module, done);
    const bump = inst._scope.get("bump");
    inst.variable({}).define("bump_copy", bump._inputs.map((i) => i._name), bump._definition);
    const text = ss_moduleCells(inst).find((c) => c.key === "bump_copy")?.text ?? "";
    if (!text.startsWith("const bump_copy ")) throw new Error(`bump_copy decompiles as ${text.slice(0, 40)}`);
    await ss_language.recompile(inst);
    const named = (n) => [...runtime._variables].filter((v) => v._module === inst && v._name === n).length;
    if (named("bump") !== 1 || named("bump_copy") !== 1) throw new Error(`bump ${named("bump")}, bump_copy ${named("bump_copy")}`);
    await Promise.all([inst.value("bump"), inst.value("bump_copy")]);
    return "bump_copy recompiles as bump_copy; one bump";
  } finally { end(); }
}
// %%
test_ss_failed_apply_changes_nothing = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // apply defines the edit and every cell it recompiles, or none of them
  let end;
  const done = new Promise((r) => (end = r));
  const snap = (m) => JSON.stringify([...runtime._variables].filter((v) => v._module === m).map((v) => [v._name, String(v._definition), v._inputs.map((i) => i._name)]));
  try {
    const inst = await ss_instance(ss_module, done);
    const v = inst._scope.get("tally");
    const source = (await ss_language.decompile([v])).replace("state(0)", "state(5)");
    if (!ss_language.check(source, [v]).ok) throw new Error("the edit to tally does not check");
    const before = snap(inst);
    ss_language.faults.afterEditDefine = inst;
    let threw = null;
    try { await ss_language.apply(source, [v]); } catch (e) { threw = e; } finally { ss_language.faults.afterEditDefine = null; }
    if (!threw) throw new Error("the injected fault did not reach apply's caller");
    if (snap(inst) !== before) throw new Error("a failed apply left the module changed");
    return `the injected fault "${threw.message}" left the module as it was`;
  } finally { end(); }
}
// %%
test_ss_instance_keeps_user_ids = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // ss_instance copies each definition as it is, so a cell's own \`id:\` property is left as written
  let end;
  const done = new Promise((r) => (end = r));
  try {
    const a = await ss_instance(ss_module, done);
    const anchor = a._scope.get("doubled");
    const made = await ss_language.apply('const tagged = () => ({ id: "anon", n: 1 });', [], { module: { module: a }, variables: [anchor] });
    if (made === undefined) throw new Error("tagged was not stored");
    const b = await ss_instance(a, done);
    const value = await b.value("tagged");
    const same = String(a._scope.get("tagged")._definition) === String(b._scope.get("tagged")._definition);
    if (value.id !== "anon" || !same) throw new Error(`value ${JSON.stringify(value)}, the copy's definition is the same text: ${same}`);
    return `tagged keeps id "anon"; the copy's definition is the same text`;
  } finally { end(); }
}
// %%
test_ss_deleted_state_is_not_inherited = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // a state cell deleted outside apply (the editor's delete button) while a cell with the same text lives in
  // another module: a new cell with that text starts from state(0), not from the deleted cell's state
  const T = "const deletedKept = (): StateCell<number> => state(0);";
  const made = [];
  const mod = async (texts) => {
    const m = runtime.module();
    made.push(m);
    m.define(soundscript.INPUTS.rejected, [], () => soundscript.rejected);
    for (const t of texts) if (await ss_language.apply(t, [], { module: { module: m } }) === undefined) throw new Error(`not stored: ${t}`);
    return m;
  };
  const frames = async (f) => { for (let i = 0; i < 600 && !(await f()); i++) await new Promise((r) => requestAnimationFrame(r)); return f(); };
  try {
    const twin = await mod([T]);
    await twin.value("deletedKept");
    const a = await mod([T, "const setKept = (deletedKept: State<number>) => action(() => deletedKept.set(7));"]);
    const set = await a.value("setKept");
    set();
    if (!(await frames(async () => (await a.value("deletedKept")) === 7))) throw new Error("deletedKept did not become 7");
    const doomed = [...runtime._variables].filter((v) => v._module === a && v._name !== soundscript.INPUTS.rejected);
    let seen;
    const deletionSeen = new Promise((r) => (seen = r));
    const off = onCodeChange(({ variable, previous }) => { if (variable === null && doomed.includes(previous?.variable)) seen(); });
    let saw = false;
    deletionSeen.then(() => (saw = true));
    try { for (const v of doomed) v.delete(); if (!(await frames(() => saw))) throw new Error("the deletion was not reported in 600 frames"); } finally { off(); }
    const b = await mod([T]);
    const start = await b.value("deletedKept");
    if (start !== 0) throw new Error(`the new deletedKept started at ${start}, the deleted cell's state`);
    return "deletedKept set to 7 and deleted outside apply, with a twin alive: a new deletedKept starts at 0";
  } finally {
    for (const m of made) for (const v of [...runtime._variables]) if (v._module === m) { soundscript.release(v._value); v.delete(); }
  }
}
// %%
//raw: test_ss_ref_handle
// %%
ss_test_results = {
  ss_tests_on;
  // a long value (an error message) is cut to one line, so the state column stays in view
  return htl.html`<div class="ss-tests">${tests({ filter: (t) => t.name.includes("@tomlarkworthy/soundscript#") })}</div>`;
}
